\par\par \b \uc2 EXCHANGE --- The Score: The Business Week in 7 Stocks\b0\par\par\uc2 By Francesca Fontana \par \uc2 687 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 January 2021\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SLACK TECHNOLOGIES INC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 WORK -0.6%\par \par \uc2 Slack had a tense start to the New Year. The workplace messaging platform suffered a widespread service disruption for several hours on Monday, as many employees returned to work for their first full workday of the year. The company said customers experienced problems loading channels and connecting to Slack, a service that many employees depend upon while working from home during the pandemic. On Dec. 14, more than a dozen of \uc2 Alphabet Inc\uc2 .'s \uc2 Google\uc2  services, including its popular email client Gmail and \uc2 YouTube\uc2 , also suffered disruptions, causing issues for workers. Slack shares fell 0.6% Monday.\par \par \uc2 ALPHABET INC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 GOOG -1.4%\par \par \uc2 Organized labor now has a beachhead inside Silicon Valley. In a rare move for America's tech epicenter, a group of employees at \uc2 Google\uc2  parent Alphabet announced Monday that they formed the Alphabet Workers Union. The union is the first one open to employees and contractors at any Alphabet company. Around 200 workers are backing it, a small fraction of the company's more than 132,000 employees. Members said the union's immediate goal is to allow employees to speak about the company without facing career repercussions. Alphabet shares fell 1.4% Monday.\par \par \uc2 FACEBOOK INC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 FB +2.1%\par \par \uc2 Facebook\uc2  is putting its foot down. On Thursday, the social-media giant banned President Trump from its platforms indefinitely in the wake of Wednesday's attack on the U.S. Capitol by a pro-Trump mob. \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and \uc2 Twitter Inc\uc2 . initially removed posts by the president Wednesday and temporarily locked the accounts that had helped propel him to power, citing the risk of violence. \uc2 Facebook\uc2  shares rose 2.1% Thursday.\par \par \uc2 TESLA INC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 TSLA +7.9%\par \par \uc2 Meet the new richest person in the world: \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 . In claiming the title this past week, the Tesla chief executive overtook \uc2 Amazon.com Inc\uc2 . leader \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2  thanks to a meteoric rise in the value of the electric-car maker. His net worth totaled around $195 billion Thursday, up from roughly $30 billion a year ago and exceeding Mr. Bezos' wealth by about $10 billion, according to the Bloomberg Billionaires Index. Both men watched shares in their companies rise during the pandemic even as the global economy took a hit. The value of Tesla's shares added 7.9% Thursday.\par \par \uc2 WALGREENS BOOTS ALLIANCE INC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 WBA +5.2%\par \par \uc2 Covid-19 fears didn't stop \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  customers from getting their prescriptions near the end of 2020. The drugstore chain on Thursday reported stronger-than-expected pharmaceutical sales in the quarter ended Nov. 30, despite some hesitancy by customers to visit its stores. Pharmacy foot traffic is down as Covid-19 precautions keep seasonal flu cases down and people skip routine medical care and in-person shopping. The company's quarterly results came a day after \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  agreed to sell most of its pharmacy wholesale unit. \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  shares rose 5.2% Thursday.\par \par \uc2 BED BATH & BEYOND INC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 BBBY -10%\par \par \uc2 Bed Bath & Beyond\uc2 's housecleaning efforts aren't yet enough to make it shine. On Thursday, the home-goods retailer reported a drop in revenue in the most recent quarter compared with the year-earlier period. The company attributed the decline in part to permanent store closures and divestitures of some brands, part of a reorganization accelerated by the pandemic. Also part of the plan is a greater emphasis on digital sales, which surged during the quarter as customers continue to shop from home to prevent the spread of Covid-19. \uc2 Bed Bath & Beyond\uc2  shares fell 10% Thursday.\par \par \uc2 SHOPIFY INC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 SHOP +6.6%\par \par \uc2 Looking for TrumpStore.com? You'll get an error message. Online stores run by the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  and Trump campaign that sell "Make America Great Again" merchandise were taken offline Thursday by the Canadian e-commerce company after Wednesday's riot at the U.S. Capitol. \uc2 Shopify\uc2  said it terminated stores affiliated with President Trump because his comments Wednesday violated a policy prohibiting retailers from promoting or supporting organizations or people that promote violence. \uc2 Shopify\uc2  shares gained 6.6% Thursday.\par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw380\pich316\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal5700\pichgoal4740
