\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 Apple CEO Cook's Pay Jumps As Remote Work Lifted Profit\b0\par\par\uc2 By Tim Higgins \par \uc2 491 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 January 2021\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Apple Inc\uc2 . said it exceeded its internal financial targets in the past fiscal year, resulting in the company paying out 179% of the targeted bonuses for named officers.\par \par \uc2 For Chief Executive \uc2 Tim Cook\uc2 , that meant his cash bonus rose 40% last year to $10.7 million, \uc2 Apple\uc2  said Tuesday in its annual proxy filing with the \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 His bonus had taken a 36% hit in 2019 when his pay package fell as revenue and profit declined tied to weaker iPhone sales.\par \par \uc2 In the past fiscal year, despite a global pandemic that disrupted economies around the world, \uc2 Apple\uc2 's profit rose 3.9% with laptops and iPads sales benefiting from workers and students stuck at home as part of efforts to slow the spread of Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 Apple\uc2 's share price rose more than 80% in 2020, placing its market value at more than $2 trillion.\par \par \uc2 In addition to his compensation, Mr. Cook had a total of $281.9 million in restricted stock that vested during the year.\par \par \uc2 Those shares were a core part of Mr. Cook's long-term incentive package that was awarded in 2011 when he became CEO.\par \par \uc2 The decadelong plan's final tranche vests later this year.\par \par \uc2 In September, \uc2 Apple\uc2 's board awarded a new long-term equity plan to Mr. Cook with shares that vest from 2023 through 2025, giving him incentive to stay on as CEO through that period. Mr. Cook, 60 years old, joined \uc2 Apple\uc2  in 1998.\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 Apple\uc2 's proxy filing, Mr. Cook's 2020 pay, excluding vested shares, totaled $14.8 million, including the cash bonus and a $3 million salary that didn't change from the prior year.\par \par \uc2 The package included $470,246 in security costs and $432,564 for air travel.\par \par \uc2 The company requires Mr. Cook to use private planes for all business and personal travel.\par \par \uc2 In the prior year, fiscal 2019, Mr. Cook's executive compensation, excluding vested shares, totaled nearly $11.6 million. His pay included a $7.7 million cash bonus, some $450,000 in security costs and $315,000 in air- travel expenses.\par \par \uc2 For the quarter ended in September, sales of computers, iPads and smartwatches helped buoy the company in the three-month period, with total revenue rising 1%.\par \par \uc2 Wall Street analysts surveyed by FactSet, on average, expected revenue to fall for the period. Revenue excluding iPhone sales rose 25% compared with a year ago, with Mac computers reaching a record of $9 billion.\par \par \uc2 That quarter's profit fell to $12.7 billion, or 73 cents a share, from $13.7 billion, or 76 cents a year earlier, the company said. The results beat analyst expectations for profit of 71 cents a share.\par \par \uc2 The results helped \uc2 Apple\uc2  conclude its fiscal year with an increase in revenue and profit after both figures fell in the previous 12-month period.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020210106eh160001v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
