\par\par \b \uc2 IBM Taps Ex-Trump Aide Cohn As Executive\b0\par\par\uc2 By Matt Grossman \par \uc2 547 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 January 2021\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 International Business Machines Corp\uc2 . appointed \uc2 Gary D. Cohn\uc2 , a former Goldman Sachs executive and economic adviser to President Trump, as its vice chairman and member of its executive leadership team as the tech company tries to revive its fortunes.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Cohn, who brings a vast Rolodex of corporate and government contacts, will work on business development, public advocacy, client services and client-relationship management, \uc2 IBM\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Cohn is joining an iconic American tech company that is undergoing a once-in-a-generation overhaul after years of struggling for growth. \uc2 IBM\uc2  has reported declining revenue in 30 quarters over the past 10 years, and its stock price has lagged rivals, even though sales remain big, at more than $70 billion a year.\par \par \uc2 IBM\uc2  appointed \uc2 Arvind Krishna\uc2  its CEO last year, announced layoffs and said it plans to split the company, carving out a large chunk of its IT-services operations that will leave the company far smaller and more focused on high-growth cloud computing business.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Krishna said Mr. Cohn's business-transformation skills would help \uc2 IBM\uc2  as it aims to accelerate its shift to cloud and artificial-intelligence businesses.\par \par \uc2 Founded in 1911, \uc2 IBM\uc2  made its name building computers and later providing technology services to other companies. But it was slow to adapt as corporations in recent years shifted from storing data on big servers they owned to using the cloud. \uc2 Amazon.com Inc\uc2 . and \uc2 Microsoft Corp\uc2 . embraced the cloud and turned it into a huge business that helped propel their growth to valuations of more than $1 trillion, or 10 times \uc2 IBM\uc2 's market valuation.\par \par \uc2 The Covid-19 pandemic has accelerated the adoption of cloud computing as companies rushed to adapt to telecommuting arrangements for their workforces, and as more people have embraced online shopping and become massive consumers of digital entertainment.\par \par \uc2 But the pandemic has also hit some areas of IT spending where \uc2 IBM\uc2  has historically been strong. In the past two quarters, IBMs cloud-computing revenue grew at a rapid year-over-year clip even as the company's overall sales declined.\par \par \uc2 The pandemic, Mr. Krishna said in May, "will accelerate what may have been a five-year journey" for the industry's transformation.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Cohn, 60 years old, served as director of the National Economic Council from Mr. Trump's inauguration from January 2017 to April 2018. He was president and chief operating officer for Goldman Sachs Group Inc. from 2006 until 2016.\par \par \uc2 He is also co-chairman of \uc2 Cohn Robbins Holdings Corp\uc2 ., a blank-check company that launched an initial public offering in September. Blank-check companies, which enjoyed a banner year in 2020, have no business operations but raise funds with the goal of merging with a private company to make the target company publicly traded.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Cohn said he would resign from his White House job shortly after Mr. Trump announced steel and aluminum tariffs that Mr. Cohn had opposed. Mr. Cohn had also criticized the president's response to white-supremacist violence in Charlottesville, Va., in the summer of 2017. Later that year, he played a key role in overseeing tax policy changes that Mr. Trump championed.\par \par \uc2 A spokeswoman for IBM said Mr. Cohn wasn't available.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020210106eh160001u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
